        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>plant_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PO:0000030</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>A septum is formed by the fusion of the walls of two adjacent organs (ovary walls or anther walls), for example, the partition between two sections of an orange, seen in cross-section.</rdfs:comment>
