        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>0.07.02 Hypocotyl emerges above soil in soybean (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BBCH growth stage 08 (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>hypocotyl and cotyledon emergence in Arabidopsis (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>hypocotyl emergence in Solanaceae (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>PO:0007043</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>This term is used only for seed plants. The actual point of emergence from the seed coat (PO:0009088) may not be observed if the seed (PO:0009010) is underneath a growth medium. In a fruit (PO:0009001) with a persistent pericarp (PO:0009084), emergence from the seed coat may not be observed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hypocotyl emergence stage</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
