        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/po#TraitNet"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Usually one of a pair of appendages. May take the form of a spine (PO:0025174) or may be bristled or brush-like. Stipules may occur on the opposite side of the shoot axis from the leaf they are associated with, but they are still thought to arise from part of the leaf.</rdfs:comment>
