        <oboInOwl:id>PO:0030030</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/po#Bryophytes"/>
        <rdfs:comment>When an archegonium occurs on a specialized lateral branch of the gametophore, all of the phyllomes on that branch are usually perichaetal bracts. If an archegonium occurs on a main axis of the gametophore, only the terminal phyllomes are usually perichaetal bracts. The two or three terminal-most perichaetal bracts may fuse to form a gametophytic perianth.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>perichaetal bract</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
